  "notes": "{空|あ}く is an intransitive godan verb meaning to become vacant or empty.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: {空|あ}ける (transitive, to vacate/empty)\n- Pattern: Xが{空|あ}く\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {空|あ}いている means 'is available/vacant/empty' (resulting state)\n- Example: {席|せき}が{空|あ}いている = The seat is available\n- Example: お{腹|なか}が{空|あ}いている = I'm hungry\n\nWATCH OUT:\n- {開|あ}く: to open (a door, lid, etc.)\n- {明|あ}く: to dawn, to end (a period)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {席|せき}が{空|あ}く: a seat becomes available\n- {部屋|へや}が{空|あ}く: a room becomes available\n- お{腹|なか}が{空|あ}く: to get hungry\n- {手|て}が{空|あ}く: to have free hands / to be available",
